  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining SM-2 Algorithm**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of implementing the SuperMemo-2 algorithm in code. The core of this SpacedRepetitionAlgorithm will involve user evaluation of recall quality, ranging from 0 (complete blackout) to 5. This feedback will be crucial in determining the appropriate intervals for future reviews. This is the first step in this process!\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_8637026490402040505"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"package com.example.srs\\n\\nimport com.example.data.model.SrsReviewEntity\\nimport kotlin.math.max\\nimport kotlin.math.roundToInt\\n\\nobject SpacedRepetitionAlgorithm {\\n    private const val ONE_DAY_MS = 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000L\\n    private const val MIN_EASE_FACTOR = 1.3f\\n\\n    /**\\n     * Applies SM-2 algorithm to compute next interval, ease factor, and due date.\\n     * @param current The current review record\\n     * @param quality Recall quality: 0 (blackout) to 5 (instant perfect recall)\\n     */\\n    fun calculateNextReview(\\n        current: SrsReviewEntity,\\n        quality: Int\\n    ): SrsReviewEntity {\\n        val clampedQuality = quality.coerceIn(0, 5)\\n        var repetition = current.repetition\\n        var intervalDays = current.intervalDays\\n        var easeFactor = current.easeFactor\\n\\n        // Calculate new ease factor\\n        val qDiff = 5 - clampedQuality\\n        val newEaseFactor = max(\\n            MIN_EASE_FACTOR,\\n            easeFactor + (0.1f - qDiff * (0.08f + qDiff * 0.02f))\\n        )\\n\\n        if (clampedQuality < 3) {\\n            // Failed recall: reset repetition count, schedule for tomorrow\\n            repetition = 0\\n            intervalDays = 1\\n        } else {\\n            // Successful recall\\n            intervalDays = when (repetition) {\\n                0 -> 1\\n                1 -> 6\\n                else -> (intervalDays * newEaseFactor).roundToInt().coerceAtLeast(1)\\n            }\\n            repetition += 1\\n        }\\n\\n        val nextTimestamp = System.currentTimeMillis() + (intervalDays * ONE_DAY_MS)\\n\\n        return current.copy(\\n            repetition = repetition,\\n            intervalDays = intervalDays,\\n            easeFactor = newEaseFactor,\\n            nextReviewTimestamp = nextTimestamp,\\n            lastQuality = clampedQuality\\n        )\\n    }\\n\\n    /**\\n     * Converts simple 4-button choice into 0-5 quality score:\\n     * - Again: 1\\n     * - Hard: 2\\n     * - Good: 4\\n     * - Easy: 5\\n     */\\n    fun gradeToQuality(grade: ReviewGrade): Int = when (grade) {\\n        ReviewGrade.AGAIN -> 1\\n        ReviewGrade.HARD -> 2\\n        ReviewGrade.GOOD -> 4\\n        ReviewGrade.EASY -> 5\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nenum class ReviewGrade(val label: String, val intervalDescription: String) {\\n    AGAIN(\\\"Again\\\", \\\"1d\\\"),\\n    HARD(\\\"Hard\\\", \\\"2d\\\"),\\n    GOOD(\\\"Good\\\", \\\"4d\\\"),\\n    EASY(\\\"Easy\\\", \\\"7d\\\")\\n}\\n\",\"Description\":\"SM-2 spaced repetition calculation engine\",\"Overwrite\":true,\"TargetFile\":\"/app/src/main/java/com/example/srs/SpacedRepetitionAlgorithm.kt\",\"toolAction\":\"Writing SpacedRepetitionAlgorithm.kt\",\"toolSummary\":\"Create Spaced Repetition engine\"}"
      thinking_signature: "\022\310\t\n\305\t\001i\024}\0236\213\341\265JDs\f*J\333\275\375*\365JR\251\235/\v\371\254A\006]\033k[\220\t;\026\210?J\0268d<\221\331e\023\006E\036\346&]}6\v\250:H\203\227\002\353\032\270\241\371}{\001\236X\220\002r\310[!\264\027-J\306U\\Y\200:\253\002h\265\341\200\244\330\200]F\227R\245O\241\351\210\r\203\201\220s\036n\352\346\320e\305\031\213\276\323\257|v\264\325\244]0\023\333\3058\031\\\033\020\214\f}\357\313W\321-M\377\210\332\231\336\275y\241\246\267\350V\342\022\202Z\350\365jM\374Y\b+\224|\272\3431G\350\355>\250\253\344W\0042\210g\312\005\307\274g\231=\350\330\310{\224F\342J\031l\351\226\26460\243\352J;\035\304A\002S\330\330\261\304\3713\376\346A\023\020\035x*\375Op\235\nP\335t\001\032\367k\306\237\fy\262=v`\304\234.78\035\222\321S\346Y\260\236Lkr\253\021\031/\004\314=>y&\362g\310g\255\035y\262+\004\365\t\342Sd09T\320\203\306R\372\333S\213C\264\367\335\000\225>\270\366K1Y\243\256\002H\367P\266 \240\322w\312\031\274C\247\036\250:\355\232)\265\020\216\006#?\355Q)\335\374\250\316\217D\216\030\257\361b\342\236X41\362[/;\341E\311\302V=\306\306\002\356\016\373\v\230\224\342\306\354\373\354\314G\270\226\277\211\363\376\202\f(X?P\344\024\310\226\311\' \025\307\320\005\272\221\364v\343\034xF\371\005\253\321\307\031_\226Kv \350\343\331\360\225\332\231e\027\376_\364\306\214]\251\325;/\364{!\337\361\006\210]\211\350U;{2b\352b\267\227\216\215\352\245^\b^~Q\016\326Z\033pp\300i\300\31422\331\026\253\026\177\317\335\335\030\265\257\274/,\337]\203\370\271\024\272Q`k\240B\016CE\221\222\024\305\246\373J6H\267nA\316\362\321a\346\250l\275Q\235n\031,\v\273&&\340\336\242+{\037\020q\366\\\313I\fpx\350\026\202Jq\232\362\313\265\251\001J\363\2032\327=&\370\032\311)\005\275\245\211&\361\035\315Y\215\300I\274\030%H\251k\334y[?\323v\315\261\f\221\231\020\302\327\215\2358\227\341\030G]\241\201\224\2222^\022\335\231\2729\325\005\323Yd\001\027M8:\221\363\346\247l\210{1w\203\372q9@\334\317\350\242\247A\374\365\004\352\371)\372Q\327Z\257\\\241\353\204\a\316\033\222