  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Adjusting Initial Grades**\n\nI\'ve been working on setting up the lesson grades with a default of 0, as you requested. The grade will now increase dynamically based on correct answers, but reduce if there are errors. I\'m focusing on the implementation of the grade increase: If a user answers 90 or more of the 100 questions correctly, the grade should be 4.5.\n\n\n**Calculating Final Grades**\n\nI\'m now calculating the final grade and considering unlocking the next lesson. I need to keep track of the last 100 answers. The grade will be calculated by taking the total count of correct answers, dividing by 100, and multiplying by 5. Additionally, I need to provide correct and incorrect word variants. I\'m focusing on providing only inner case words, excluding capital-case words.\n\n\n**Clarifying Planning Mode**\n\nI\'m now clarifying the planning mode trigger conditions. It seems the system should trigger if the user explicitly requests a plan or when \"planning mode\" is activated in the metadata. I\'m investigating how this operates in a 2-turn flow, asking clarifying questions in Turn 1, but I need to ensure I understand when to ask questions vs. present a plan directly, based on the user\'s intent within the metadata section.\n\n\n**Refining Grade Logic**\n\nI\'m now refining the grade logic and clarifying some details. The default grade remains at 0, not 4.5. Lesson unlocking depends on achieving a grade of 4.5 or higher, based on the last 100 answers, or the total if fewer than 100 have been answered. The grade calculation formula is a ratio of correct answers divided by 100 (or total answers if fewer than 100), multiplied by 5.\n\n\n"
