  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Initiating Phase 3 Execution**\n\nI\'m now in Phase 3, executing the plan, with the user\'s approval. I\'m focusing on the specifics of implementing the dynamic grading and progression system for the 100-answer lessons. I\'ve noted the change; all lessons now begin with a default grade of 0.0, not 4.5. I\'m also reviewing the grade formula to ensure accuracy and consistency.\n\n\n**Refining Grade Calculation**\n\nI\'ve finalized the grade formula: `(correctCount / 100.0f) * 5.0f`. Now, I\'m focusing on the data structure, implementing a `LessonAnswerEntity` in Room to track the last 100 answers for each lesson. This includes `id`, `lessonId`, `isCorrect`, and `timestamp`. Achieving 90 or more correct answers in the last 100 will trigger a grade of 4.5 or higher and mark the lesson as complete, unlocking the next. Both Sentence Practice and Vocabulary Drills will contribute to this data. I\'m noting that Lesson 1 is always unlocked.\n\n\n**Implementing Lowercase Validation**\n\nI\'m now implementing the lowercase requirement for sentence construction words. I\'ll modify the tile pool to use strictly lowercase words. I\'ll also strip punctuation from the chips and perform lowercase-insensitive equality checks during submission. I\'m focusing on the necessary data structure modifications, like the introduction of a new `LessonAnswerEntity` and corresponding DAO methods. I plan to add appropriate default values for `masteryScore`, `isCompleted`, and add an `isUnlocked` variable to the `LessonEntity`. I\'ll also register `LessonAnswerEntity` in the database.\n\n\n**Updating Data Handling**\n\nI\'m now integrating the data handling changes. I\'ll modify `ensureInitialDataLoaded()` to confirm that Lesson 1 is unlocked with initial scores set to 0.0f, and that subsequent lessons are locked. I\'ll also add a `recordAnswer()` function to the `CurriculumRepository` to store answers, maintain a 100-answer history, calculate scores, update lesson mastery scores, and unlock the next lesson when the score hits the threshold. In the `InitialCurriculumData`, I will ensure all lessons start with masteryScore of 0f and are incomplete.\n\n\n**Displaying Dynamic Grades**\n\nI\'m now implementing the UI updates. I plan to show the current lesson grade, lock status, and progress in `CurriculumScreen.kt`. In `LessonDetailScreen.kt`, I will display the live score and answer count like \"45/100 correct answers, grade 2.3\". I\'ll also modify `SentencePracticeScreen.kt` to strip capitals and punctuation, and I\'ll add the necessary `viewModel.recordAnswer()` calls in both `SentencePracticeScreen.kt` and `VocabDrillScreen.kt` when the user submits their answer.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_7265496301889246929"
