  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Score Display**\n\nI\'ve been examining the score display logic, specifically lines 304-308. I\'m focusing on the conditional formatting for `displayScore`. It appears the code prioritizes `lesson.masteryScore` if it\'s above zero, formatting it to one decimal place. Otherwise, it defaults to using `lesson.orderIndex`. I\'m starting to consider if this logic fully addresses the request and considering different scenarios.\n\n\n**Refining Grade Calculation**\n\nI\'m now revising the grade calculation strategy. The default grade should indeed be zero, not 4.5. It will increment with correct answers and decrement with errors. A score of 4.5 unlocks the next lesson. I\'ll maintain the most recent 100 answers, determining the grade as (correct answers / 100) * 5. I am planning the update `LessonStreamCard` in `CurriculumScreen.kt`. I\'ve outlined the logic for both locked and unlocked lessons, including visual cues and user messaging based on completion status.\n\n\n"
