  planner_response {
    response: "### Summary of Changes\n\n1. **100-Answer Dynamic Grading & Progression Gate**:\n   - Initialized all lessons with a default grade of `0.0` (instead of `4.5`).\n   - Implemented a persistent rolling history of the user\'s last 100 answers per lesson in Room (`LessonAnswerEntity`).\n   - The grade is computed dynamically on each answer as `(correctAnswersInLast100 / 100.0) * 5.0`.\n   - Both **Sentence Practice** and **Vocabulary Drills** actively record correct and incorrect answers to this pool.\n   - Reaching **90 or more correct answers out of 100** awards a grade of `4.5` (or higher), marks the lesson as completed, and unblocks the next lesson.\n   - Locked lessons display a lock icon and required score indicator, while Lesson 1 is unlocked by default.\n\n2. **Morphological Word Variants (Distractors)**:\n   - Enriched sentence practice word pools with correct tokens plus wrong grammatical variants (e.g. contrasting person forms like *\321\200\320\260\320\264\320\270\320\274 / \321\200\320\260\320\264\320\270\321\210 / \321\200\320\260\320\264\320\270*, tense variants like *\321\200\320\260\320\264\320\270\321\233\321\203 / \321\200\320\260\320\264\320\270\320\276*, and case inflections).\n   - Enriched vocabulary matching drills with plausible grammatical distractors.\n\n3. **Inner-Case (Lowercase) Word Bank Chips**:\n   - Normalized all word chips in the tile pool and assembly bay to strictly lower case (\"inner case\").\n   - Stripped punctuation from word chips so capitalized letters or trailing periods/question marks do not reveal the sentence opener or closer.\n   - Validation compares cleaned lowercase tokens without punctuation bias."
